            <ArticleTitle>Multiple coronary artery dissections in a woman at term.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of acute myocardial infarction caused by multiple coronary artery dissections in a pregnant woman at term. When reinfarction elicited fetal distress, Caesarean section was performed under carefully administered extradural anaesthesia, with maternal and fetal survival.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
